    "title": "South Florida Defeats Tulane 97-83",
    "text": "• South Florida defeated Tulane 97-83 on Wednesday night.\n• Wes Enis scored 25 points for South Florida.\n• Enis shot 7 of 13 from the field, 5 of 10 from 3-point range, and 6 of 7 from the free-throw line.\n• Joseph Pinion scored 17 points for South Florida.\n• Pinion shot 6 of 12 from the field (3 of 8 from 3-point range) and had six rebounds.\n• Izaiyah Nelson scored 11 points for South Florida.\n• Nelson shot 3 of 10 from the field and 5 of 8 from the free-throw line.\n• Tyler Ringgold and Asher Woods each scored 14 points for Tulane.\n• Rowan Brumbaugh scored 12 points, had six rebounds, and five assists for Tulane.\n• South Florida (14-7, 6-2 American Athletic Conference) took the lead with 7:51 remaining in the first half and did not trail again.\n• South Florida led 52-39 at halftime.\n• South Florida extended its lead to 68-48 during the second half with a 10-0 scoring run.\n• The Associated Press used technology from Data Skrive and data from Sportradar to create this story.",
    "summary": "NEW ORLEANS (AP) — Wes Enis scored 25 points as South Florida beat Tulane 97-83 on Wednesday night. Enis shot 7 of 13 from the field, including 5 for 10 from 3-point range, and went 6 for 7 from the free-throw line for the Bulls (14-7, 6-2 American Athletic Conference). Izaiyah Nelson shot 3 of 10 from the field and 5 of 8 from the free-throw line to finish with 11 points. The Green Wave (12-9, 3-5) were led in scoring by Tyler Ringgold and Asher Woods, who finished with 14 points apiece.",
